- core/stats/curves.py:
  - x_transform_regression: SLR on w = f(x + c) for log10, ln, sqrt,
    square, exp and reciprocal (Fig. 17.1); predictions and CIs on the
    original x scale, comparison of all admissible transformations by
    adjusted R², AIC and SBC (Example 17.1A).
  - polynomial_regression: order 1–10 in raw, centred or orthogonal
    powers; sequential ANOVA (Table 17.3), parameters in simple powers
    (Table 17.4), VIF, warning when the highest term is not significant,
    lack of fit against pure error, curve with CI on a dense grid,
    extrapolation warning (Example 17.1B).
  - trigonometric_regression: known period, 1–5 harmonics; amplitude and
    phase with delta-method SEs, times of maximum and minimum
    (Example 17.2, Table 17.6).
- Tests against Tables 17.2–17.4, 17.6, 17.12 and Examples 17.1A, 17.2
  (Tables 17.1, 17.5 data added).
- Catalog, i18n, bridge (xy kind, curve plot), messages.

